\u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"2\">2: \u003Cspan>Miller: Απέλ̣&lt;λ&gt;ι̣[[ν]]ν\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>",{"id":276,"html":277},"translation","\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>[...] Myskon, son of Damis son of Kobetos [...] Anthemokritos bade Apellis offer security [...] said [...] was; he came upon [...] of the Leontines [...] Myskon sitting along the avenue [...] came (not?) having the money, the price of the cattle; he did not buy [...] went to Empedokles, son of Mnasimachos [...] let [...] become (liable?) to act as surety (trans. by Miller).\u003C/p>  ",{"id":276,"html":279},"\u003Ch2>Italian translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>[...] Myskon, figlio di Damis figlio di Kobetos [...] Anthemokritos ordinò ad Apelis(?) di agire da garante [...] disse [...] era; si imbatté [...] dei Leontini [...] Myskon seduto lungo il viale [...] venne (non?) avendo il denaro, il prezzo del bestiame; non comprò [...] andò da Empedokles, figlio di Mnasimachos [...] lasciò che [...] diventasse garante.\u003C/p>  ",{"id":281,"html":282},"commentary","\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The text appears on the obverse of an opisthographic lamina with a defixio on the reverse (ISic030019, Arena II(2), no. 45, Curbera no.13).\u003C/p>  ",{"id":284,"html":285},"bibliography","\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Miller 1973 fig. p. 37 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002516\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002516\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Brugnone 1980-1981 437-438 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001462\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001462\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Arena